  <static seed="19" source="Library/PCC/BasicAlgebra/Factoring/factoring115.pg">
    <statement><p>Factor the given polynomial</p>
<p><m>{2x\mathopen{}\left(x+y\right)-5\mathopen{}\left(x+y\right)}=</m> <fillin characters="19" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>If the expression cannot be factored then answer with <alert>prime</alert>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(2x-5\right)\mathopen{}\left(x+y\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The greatest common factor to both terms is <m>x+y</m>, so we can factor the polynomial using the 
<em>factor by grouping</em> method as follows:</p>
<p><m>{2x\mathopen{}\left(x+y\right)-5\mathopen{}\left(x+y\right)}={\left(2x-5\right)\mathopen{}\left(x+y\right)}</m></p>
<p>Note that this answer can be checked by using the FOIL (<alert>F</alert>irst <alert>O</alert>utside <alert>I</alert>nside <alert>L</alert>ast) technique (exercise).</p>
</solution>
